---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import PackageCard from '../../components/PackageCard.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
import { packages } from '../../data/packages';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Four packages, one Neura Pod platform"
  description="The Neura Pod is a modular battery and inverter unit. Four configurations ship today: Starter, Family, Commercial, and Commercial Plus. EV-ready from day one."
  canonicalPath="/products/"
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="Products"
    headline="Four systems built on one Neura Pod platform."
    subhead="Kenya's grid is becoming more distributed. Precifarm's operating answer is the Neura Pod, a modular battery and inverter unit carrying inverter, router, and battery storage in a single replaceable enclosure. EV-ready from day one. Capacity upgrades happen by swapping the Pod, not by rewiring the property."
    badges={[
      'EPRA-licensed installation',
      'Five-year service commitment',
      'Written design before you commit',
      'One-year workmanship warranty',
    ]}
  />

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="container-page section">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 md:gap-7">
        {packages.map((pkg) => (
          <PackageCard pkg={pkg} layout="detailed" />
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EV-readiness positioning -->
  <section class="bg-navy-dark text-white">
    <div class="container-page section">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-16 items-center">
        <div class="lg:col-span-5">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] font-semibold text-amber mb-4">EV-readiness</p>
          <h2 class="text-h2-sm md:text-h1 text-white leading-[1.1]">The same Pod that powers a building today charges a vehicle tomorrow.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-5 text-lg text-white/85 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            Africa's vehicle fleet is electrifying. Two-wheeler operators, light commercial fleets, and institutional vehicles are moving to battery propulsion. The charging infrastructure is not yet there to match.
          </p>
          <p>
            Precifarm's Neura Pod architecture is EV-ready from day one. The same Pod that powers a home, an SME, or a clinic today is the Pod that charges a vehicle tomorrow. Capacity upgrades happen by swapping the Pod, not by tearing up the installation.
          </p>
          <p>
            Distributed solar, distributed storage, and distributed charging form the operating thesis. The grid does not need to deliver the charge. The Pod stores it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BESS consultancy and EPC -->
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="container-page section">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Battery storage capability</p>
        <h2 class="text-h2-sm md:text-h1 text-navy-dark leading-[1.1]">Battery energy storage consultancy and EPC, sized up to approximately 10 MWh.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8 lg:gap-12">
        <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-5 text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            Battery storage is becoming a separate utility asset class. Commercial and industrial sites in Kenya are deploying battery energy storage systems for peak shaving, backup, and integration of on-site solar with the grid.
          </p>
          <p>
            Precifarm operates a battery energy storage system consultancy and EPC line, sized from a few hundred kilowatt-hours up to approximately 10 MWh of installed capacity. The scope covers feasibility analysis, system sizing, hardware specification, EPRA-licensed installation, commissioning, and operations and maintenance under the same engineering team that designed the system.
          </p>
          <p>
            Storage is treated as infrastructure. The unit of attention is uptime and dispatch behaviour against the customer's load profile, not headline kilowatt-hour figures.
          </p>
        </div>
        <aside class="rounded-card border border-hairline bg-paper p-6 md:p-7 self-start">
          <p class="eyebrow text-text-muted mb-4">BESS scope</p>
          <dl class="space-y-4 text-sm">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-text-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">Sizing</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-ink font-semibold">A few hundred kWh up to ~10 MWh installed</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-text-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">Use cases</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-ink">Peak shaving, backup, solar-grid integration</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-text-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">Delivery</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-ink">Feasibility, sizing, EPC, commissioning, O&amp;M</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-text-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">Engagement</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-ink">
                <a href="/contact/" class="text-navy font-semibold hover:underline">Brief an engineer</a>
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-paper">
    <div class="container-page section">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-3">How we price</p>
        <h2 class="text-h2-sm md:text-h1 text-navy-dark">A firm starting price, then a written quote after the site survey.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
          The side-by-side specification table lives on the homepage. Below is how Precifarm pricing is structured and what every starting price actually covers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 max-w-5xl">
        <div class="rounded-card bg-white border border-hairline p-6">
          <p class="eyebrow text-navy mb-3">How we price</p>
          <h3 class="text-h3 text-navy-dark mb-3">A firm starting price up front.</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
            Starter and Family carry firm starting prices because the standard configuration covers most homes. Commercial and Commercial Plus carry a "from" price, with a written quote issued after the site survey.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-card bg-white border border-hairline p-6">
          <p class="eyebrow text-navy mb-3">What is included</p>
          <h3 class="text-h3 text-navy-dark mb-3">Hardware, installation, and five years of service.</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
            Every starting price covers tier-1 hardware, EPRA-licensed installation, the one-year workmanship warranty, and the five-year service commitment from the same regional engineering team.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-card bg-callout-green border border-green p-6">
          <p class="eyebrow text-green mb-3">Compare like for like</p>
          <h3 class="text-h3 text-navy-dark mb-3">Hardware-only quotes look cheaper than ours.</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
            A hardware-only quote will typically come in below ours at the install. Most of that saving is the absent five-year service. Ask any installer whether the price they quote includes the engineer that returns in year three.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    variant="default"
    headline="Tell us about the room, the home, or the building."
    body="We will reply with a sized recommendation and a written quote within two business days. No commitment, no pressure."
    primaryCta={{ href: '/contact/', label: 'Get a quote' }}
    badges={['Free site assessment', 'Written design and pricing', 'Two-business-day reply']}
  />
</BaseLayout>
